// BUG REPRO (bare string for entity): `Tool2::request{ input.mode: ... }`
// declares `input.mode : Drupe::Tool2_Input_mode` (an enum entity type),
// but the pattern binds it to the bare string literal `"read"`. A String is
// not an entity value — even though `"read"` happens to be a permitted enum id,
// the entity literal would have to be written `Drupe::Tool2_Input_mode::"read"`.
// The field-argument type check (`check_arg_type`) should reject this with
// expected `entity:Tool2_Input_mode` vs actual `string`.
//
// This is the most insidious variant: the string looks right to a human but is
// the wrong *type*. The type-checker enforces this for `==`/`!=` operands, but
// currently skips predicate `input.<field>` patterns, so it validates cleanly
// when it should be rejected — and silently never matches a real Tool2 event.
//
// Expected: rejected at `validate` by the temporal type-checker.
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Tool1", resource)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Tool2"::request{
        input.mode: "read"
    }
};
